{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The deviation is established on this trip's own evidence. The trace measures 23.97 km against a booked optimal of 18.0 km, an excess of 5.97 km or 33.17%, which passes both POL-RD-01 tests at once: greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms and greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km. No clause of POL-RD-01 saves the driver once that test is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 fixes the governing measurement as gps_trace.trace_distance_km, which is 23.97 km, not the rounded 24.0 km convenience copy on the trip record. The excess to be worked is therefore 5.97 km, and trip_record.actual_distance_km may not be cited for the threshold test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 241 fixes at a 10 second sample interval, 100% coverage, zero gaps, max_gap_sec of 0.0 and no straight-line jump approaching 500 m. Limbs (a) to (c) are not engaged, so no independent corroboration is required and the deviation stands on the trace itself.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "point_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-11 has no application and the rider is not confined to a pass-through-only remedy. The POL-RD-02 recomputation is the governing arithmetic for this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Run the POL-RD-02 arithmetic on its separate lines: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 km = 13.50 + 0.28 x 30 min = 8.40) x 1.6 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 of on-optimal-route ERP = 44.42. Charged_total = 58.10. Refund = 58.10 - 44.42 = 13.68, rounded UP to SGD 13.70. That is 23.5% of the charge, far above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The recomputation preserves the 1.6 surge the rider has accepted, applying it to base, distance and time only and not to the 4.50 of ERP. That is why the refund of 13.68 tracks the excess distance alone rather than stripping out the surge the rider agreed to pay, and why the rider does not seek the full contested amount.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.surge_uplift",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory exonerates this detour. EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING - it carries no payload, a weight_multiplier of 0.0 and the issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - and no advisory in the pool names the AYE, the PIE or the Alexandra corridor in the 18:36-19:20 window. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic_advisory naming a road the optimal route traverses; with none on file the clause cannot run, and the driver's 'AYE was crawling' assertion exonerates nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00114-01", "EV-CHAT-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-04 is unavailable. The whole chat log is two messages: the rider asking 'adam road?? jurong is the other way' and the driver replying 'AYE jam boss, this way faster'. Neither is a rider instruction to take a named road; the rider's message is a query and the driver's is his own claim of congestion. Both messages carry waypoint_hint null, so there is no resolved waypoint to corroborate and nothing here transfers the cost of the detour to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-05 cannot be run. pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so there is no amended endpoint and no re-quote against which a smaller excess could be measured. Nothing in the record reduces the 5.97 km excess or displaces the 18.0 km baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-12 does not bite. vehicle_type is RYDE_X and not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null. The 18.0 km booked optimal is the correct baseline and no co-rider collection or set-down distance falls to be excluded from the excess.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The burden has shifted and the driver has not discharged it. Under POL-RD-08 the rider shows the artifacts describe the same trip - matching trip identifier and a consistent pickup and ride window across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown - and an excess over the POL-RD-01 threshold. The driver must then point to a specific artifact and a specific clause; he points to none. His counterparty statement and his chat reply name no advisory ID, and his own words ('I went up and over on the PIE. Longer on the map but it moved') concede the longer route without excusing it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00114", "EV-GPS-00114", "EV-FARE-00114", "EV-CHAT-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider is not a serial claimant and no extra corroboration is demanded of her. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1, nowhere near the 4-or-more claims with 1-or-fewer substantiated that POL-RD-08 requires before imposing a corroboration requirement beyond the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-09(1) governs the ERP lines and the rider does not double-count them. The 2.50 Kim Keat Link gantry lies on the optimal route and is properly included inside the recomputed fare; the 2.00 Adam Road gantry is off the optimal route and is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund, so it must NOT be added on top of the 13.70. The trace passes within 250 m of both gantries - nearest fixes at 0.0 m and 8.76 m - so neither line is a phantom charge under POL-RD-09(4).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-GPS-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 13.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation case from Bugis to Jurong East, and it is decidable on the record. The deviation is established. POL-RD-01 measures it on the GPS trace, which governs over the rounded 24.0 km convenience copy on the trip record: the trace is 23.97 km against the 18.0 km booked optimal — an excess of 5.97 km, or 33.17% — which clears both establishment limbs (more than 0.8 km and more than 20%). The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (241 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps), so POL-RD-07 requires no independent corroboration, and the excess is below both materiality limits (50% and 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 driver-profile consequence attaches — in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 412 completed trips (0.24%), so no repeat-deviation pattern exists, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no driver-conduct referral arises. Nothing excuses the excess. POL-RD-03 requires a traffic advisory: the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-00114-01, is MISSING — weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload — and no advisory covers the AYE, PIE or Alexandra corridor in the 18:36-19:20 window, so the clause cannot run; its absence is citable but carries no fact and does not hold the case open. POL-RD-04 is unavailable (the two chat messages contain no rider instruction and no resolved waypoint), POL-RD-05 is unavailable (pickup and dropoff unamended), and POL-RD-12 does not bite (RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL). On the driver's escalation argument: POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged. It fires where an exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited artifact that is absent; the congestion claim names no artifact and cites no advisory ID, as the pre-pass records, and the driver's own statement concedes 'no advisory that I know of'. POL-RD-08 governs that: a general assertion that traffic was bad, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, does not discharge the shifted burden, and an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight. The driver's admission that the route was 'longer on the map' is accepted as a concession of the longer route, but it concedes the route without excusing it. The money, on separate lines: charged_total = SGD 58.10. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 = 13.50 distance + 0.28 x 30 = 8.40 time) x 1.6 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 on-optimal-route ERP = SGD 44.42. Refund = 58.10 - 44.42 = SGD 13.68, above the SGD 0.50 de-minimis and below the 90% full-refund share, rounded up to SGD 13.70. The 1.6 surge the rider accepts is preserved in the recomputation. The SGD 2.00 Adam Road gantry is off the optimal route and is already comprehended inside this figure under POL-RD-09(1) — itemised, not added on top — and the trace passes within 250 m of both gantries, so neither line is phantom and no billing-integrity referral arises. The rider's pleaded 'extra 6 km' and SGD 15.00 exceed the governing 5.97 km and the SGD 13.70 the arithmetic supports. Confidence 0.9, above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation applies; no clause produces a referral, and no driver compensation is due, the distance billed (24.0 km) not being less than the trace's 23.97 km."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
